jx1 License
===========

jx1 is a Java port of the ZX1 data compression format and algorithm, with a
resumable 68000 decompressor and related experiments. It follows the dual
licensing structure of the original ZX1 (see c/zx1/LICENSE and the License
section of c/zx1/README.md):

1. THE COMPRESSOR - the Java compressor and optimal parser (Block, Optimizer,
   Compressor, Jx1, and the retired compressor experiments), derived from
   Einar Saukas' optimal C compressor - is available under the BSD 3-Clause
   License below. In practice this is relevant only if you modify its source
   code and/or incorporate the compressor within your own products; if you
   just execute it to compress files, you can simply ignore these conditions.

2. THE DECOMPRESSORS - the Java Decompressor/Djx1, the 68000 decompressors
   in 68k/ (jx1_68000.S and jx1_68000_ring.S), and the retired decompressor
   variants in retired/68k/ (including jx1_68000_ring_mod.S) - can be used
   freely within your own programs (for any platform), even for commercial
   releases. The only
   condition is that you must indicate somehow in your documentation that
   you have used ZX1/jx1.

Attribution
-----------

* The ZX1 data compression format and algorithm was designed and implemented
  by Einar Saukas (Copyright (c) 2021), with thanks to introspec/spke. The
  original C and z80 sources are vendored unmodified under c/zx1/ with their
  own LICENSE.
* The additions and differences to the original (custom buffer/backreference
  sizes, the incremental ring buffer, resumable decompression, the 68000
  target, and the direction of the optimization campaign - see README.md) are
  Copyright (c) 2026 Robbert van Dalen.
* The jx1 code and experiments - the Java port, the 68000 decompressor
  variants, the emulation/measurement rigs, and the documentation of the
  optimization campaign (retired/) - were written by Claude (Anthropic's
  Claude Code), under the direction of Robbert van Dalen.

